  "risks": [
    "STANDARD ELECTROLYTIC DATASHEETS EXPLICITLY EXCLUDE THIS DUTY. SamYoung's NXH sheet (and most general-purpose Al electrolytic sheets) state: 'The electrolytic capacitor is not suitable for circuits in which charge and discharge are frequently repeated... capacitance may drop, or the capacitor may be damaged.' Mitigating: the bank only swings 48->40 V (never to zero), peak is 2.6 A into >=2720 uF (0.65 A/can, ~0.96 mA per uF), and computed rms is 7-8x below the derated rating - nothing like photoflash duty. Still the one caveat to put in front of the human, and the reason to buy the 10000 h AEC-Q200 part over the 2000 h generic at the same price.",
    "NO JLC BASIC PART EXISTS in 100 V aluminium electrolytic OR 100 V 1210 MLCC - verified, --basic-only returns 0 results in both categories. Every part in this block is Extended, so JLC's per-part setup fee applies; at 4-6 boards that fee can exceed the parts.",
    "THT PROCESS. Radial cans land in the same process question as the reverse-mounted sockets (requirements section 7 / open question 6). Default (a), hand-solder, makes the THT bank free of process risk. If the answer moves to full SMD assembly, switch to the SMD composition and accept 2000 h endurance or 13 parts.",
    "HEIGHT vs AN UNDEFINED CEILING. Open question 5's default is 30 mm; the primary bank uses 27.0 mm of it. Below ~28 mm use the runner-up (22.0 mm). Below ~20 mm nothing in the 2800 uF/100 V class fits and the bank must go sideways (13 x 220 uF SMD at 16.5-21 mm) or the energy budget must come down.",
    "SINGLE SOURCE at the 680 uF/D18x25 value (Ymin LKM and Ymin OLKJ only, and OLKJ stock is 290). Mitigation: the D18 / 7.5 mm-pitch FOOTPRINT is multi-source at 470 uF (Ymin, SamYoung C2835738, Rubycon C1582113, NCC C705509). LAY OUT 6 x D18/7.5 mm POSITIONS AND POPULATE 4 - that second-sources the whole bank and gives the architect a capacitance knob without a respin.",
    "MLCC DC BIAS IS NOT OPTIONAL ARITHMETIC. 10 uF reads 2.7 uF at 48 V and 2.1 uF at 57 V (Murata's own chart). Anyone budgeting '40 uF of ceramic' actually has ~11 uF.",
    "KEEPOUT. No aluminium electrolytics in (2,46)-(36,68) - 748 mm2 of prime central area. MLCC and polymer are not aluminium electrolytics by the letter of the rule, but the rule exists because of a 1.25 W hot spot 11 mm below; keep life-sensitive parts out regardless.",
    "VENT ORIENTATION. D18 cans carry a top pressure-relief vent. In a sealed plastic box a vent event dumps electrolyte inside the enclosure - keep the vents pointed away from the LED wiring and the connectors, and note the 3.13 J stored-energy silkscreen warning (section 8.3).",
    "NO DATASHEET URL ON LCSC for C54915544, C46550452 (jieerrui 100 V polymer) and C49215602 (KYET film). Their ripple/ESR/endurance figures above come from the LCSC parametric attributes only. None is recommended, but P3 must obtain a real datasheet before any of them enters a BOM."
  ],
